{"name":"Aquarius","hex":"#2db0ce","fetched":"2026-11-01","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Aquarius","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A constellation of the zodiac, traditionally figured in the shape of a man (now also as a woman) carrying water.","The zodiac sign for the water carrier, ruled by Uranus or Saturn, covering January 20 – February 18 (tropical astrology) or February 15 – March 14 (sidereal astrology)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone with an Aquarius star sign"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Aquarius"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aquarius (astrology)","blocks":[{"text":"Aquarius is the eleventh astrological sign in the zodiac, originating from the constellation Aquarius. Under the tropical zodiac, the Sun is in the Aquarius sign between about January 20 and February 19. Aquarius is one of the three air signs, alongside Gemini and Libra. The ruling planets of Aquarius are Saturn, and Uranus. It is the fixed air sign. The opposite sign of Aquarius is Leo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Aquarius_symbol_%28bold%29.svg/330px-Aquarius_symbol_%28bold%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquarius_(astrology)","wikidata":"Q162119"},{"title":"Age of Aquarius","blocks":[{"text":"In astrology, the Age of Aquarius is either the current or forthcoming astrological age, depending on the method of calculation. Astrologers maintain that an astrological age is a product of the Earth's slow precessional rotation and lasts for 2,160 years, on average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/7_Chakras.JPG/330px-7_Chakras.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Aquarius","wikidata":"Q1569944"},{"title":"Aquarius (constellation)","blocks":[{"text":"Aquarius is an equatorial constellation of the zodiac, between Capricornus and Pisces. Its name is Latin for \"water-carrier\" or \"cup-carrier\", and its traditional astrological symbol is  (♒︎), a representation of water. Aquarius is one of the oldest of the recognized constellations along the zodiac. It was one of the 48 constellations listed by the 2nd-century astronomer Ptolemy, and it remains one of the 88 modern constellations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Aquarius_IAU.svg/330px-Aquarius_IAU.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquarius_(constellation)","wikidata":"Q10576"},{"title":"Aquarius (Tinashe album)","blocks":[{"text":"Aquarius is the debut studio album by American singer Tinashe. It was released on October 3, 2014, through RCA Records. In 2011, after the disbandment of the girl group the Stunners, Tinashe announced that she would begin pursuing a solo career. The following year, she released her debut mixtape, titled In Case We Die (2012). After raising her profile with the mixtape, Tinashe met with RCA, where she subsequently signed a recording contract. Following her signing a record deal, Tinashe immediately began working on the album. During the recording process, she released two other mixtapes, Reverie (2012) and Black Water (2013)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Tinashe_-_Aquarius.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquarius_(Tinashe_album)","wikidata":"Q17507554"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Aquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg/500px-Aquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Aquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg/1280px-Aquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Aquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg/500px-Aquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAquarius_Astrological_Sign_at_the_Wisconsin_State_Capitol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Clock_of_San_Marco_clockface.png/330px-Clock_of_San_Marco_clockface.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Clock_of_San_Marco_clockface.png/330px-Clock_of_San_Marco_clockface.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClock_of_San_Marco_clockface.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Aquarius2.jpg/120px-Aquarius2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Aquarius2.jpg/250px-Aquarius2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Aquarius2.jpg/120px-Aquarius2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAquarius2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/7_Chakras.JPG/330px-7_Chakras.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/7_Chakras.JPG/330px-7_Chakras.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Age of Aquarius symbol: Leonardo da Vinci's Vitruvian 